00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.030 align:start position:0%
it was just after midday in the occupied  west bank city of nablus when israeli  special forces along with domestic  security agency shin bet carried out the  raid  according to witnesses undercover troops  used a taxi with palestinian license  plates pulled up next to a car and  opened fire spraying it with bullets in  broad daylight  after the israeli forces left people  gathered to see what happened no one  suspected the vehicles were carrying the  israeli soldiers simply because of the  palestinian number plates the israeli  soldiers continued to fire for a minute  they fired more than 80 bullets and the  young palestinian men were killed on the  spot  the palestinian men were accused of  involvement in recent attacks against  israeli soldiers and civilians the  troops were filmed taking weapons from  the vehicle before they left the scene  a case of extrajudicial killings  according to the palestinian authority  that requires an international  investigation family members gathered  outside the morgue to share their  sadness and anger along with members of  the community  my son has been hunted by the israelis  for months the israeli intelligence  called for my children and threatened  them for my son to give himself in  israel's defense minister benny gantz  commended his security forces for the  operation prime minister naftali bennett  says there is no immunity for terrorists  i am really sad not only for this crime  but for the entire situation the  palestinian people have been in for  decades  we are used to these crimes but we must  act in response  i am really sad we are filled with anger  but no one is lending us a helping hand  the al-aqsa martyrs brigade the armed  wing of the fatah party says it will  retaliate  three more young men caught up in a  seemingly never-ending cycle of violence  andrew chappelle al jazeera
 

